---
source: crates/mrq-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "stdout_of(&[name, \"--help\"])"
---
Select parts of documents

Usage: mrq query [OPTIONS] <QUERY> [PATH]...

Arguments:
  <QUERY>
          The query (Markdown selector by default)

  [PATH]...
          Files, directories, globs, or `-` for stdin

Options:
      --css
          Interpret QUERY as a CSS-style selector

      --jq
          Interpret QUERY as a jq program over the JSON AST

  -o, --output <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - md:   Markdown
          - json: Nodes with source positions
          - text: Plain text content
          
          [default: md]

  -e, --exit-status
          Exit 1 if nothing matches in any input

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --config <PATH>
          Use this config file instead of discovering `.mrq.yaml`

      --flavor <FLAVOR>
          Markdown flavor [default: frontmatter `mrq.flavor`, then config, then gfm]

          Possible values:
          - commonmark: Strict CommonMark
          - gfm:        GitHub Flavored Markdown
          - obsidian:   Obsidian: gfm + wikilinks, embeds, callouts, tags, math, comments
          - mkdocs:     MkDocs: gfm + admonitions, heading attributes, definition lists, math

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colors

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colors when writing to a terminal and NO_COLOR is unset
          - always: Always emit colors
          - never:  Never emit colors
          
          [default: auto]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Diagnostics output format [default: human, or github when GITHUB_ACTIONS=true]

          Possible values:
          - human:  Human-readable, with source snippets
          - json:   A single JSON array
          - ndjson: One JSON object per line
          - sarif:  SARIF 2.1.0
          - github: GitHub Actions workflow annotations

  -q, --quiet...
          Print less output; repeat for even less

  -v, --verbose...
          Print more output; repeat for even more
